# ViForge — Forging Small Models into Specialists

> **ViForge** is an open-source, modular post-training experimentation framework designed to systematically specialize cost-efficient base language models into high-performing domain experts (starting with **DeepSeek V4 Pro** in **Software Engineering**).

---

## 1. The Core Research Hypothesis

> **"Can specialization improve the software-engineering capability of a cost-efficient model enough to make it a better capability-per-dollar choice than larger frontier alternatives?"**

ViForge enforces rigorous empirical Pareto-optimality analysis across:
$$\text{Capability-per-Dollar} = \frac{\Delta \mathcal{S}_{\text{domain}} - \lambda \cdot \max(0, -\Delta \mathcal{S}_{\text{general}})}{\mathcal{C}_{\text{train}} + \mathcal{C}_{\text{infer}}(N_{\text{tokens}})}$$

```text
GENERALIST MODEL (e.g. DeepSeek V4 Pro)
       │
       ▼
   DATA / TASK SPECIFICATION
       │
       ▼
 ┌────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │                ViForge                 │
 │                                        │
 │  • SFT (Instruction Tuning)            │
 │  • LoRA / QLoRA (NF4 4-bit)            │
 │  • Continual Pretraining (DAPT)        │
 │  • Preference Alignment (DPO / GRPO)   │
 │  • Synthetic Teacher Distillation      │
 │  • Contamination & Security Shield     │
 └────────────────────────────────────────┘
       │
       ▼
SPECIALIST MODEL
       │
       ▼
QUALITY × RETENTION × COST PARETO EVALUATION
```

---

## 2. Key Architectural Features

* **Pre-Flight Feasibility & Memory Profiler:** Analytically computes VRAM requirements across weights, gradients, optimizer states, and activations with a 15% safety headroom before allocating GPU infrastructure.
* **Data Governance & Contamination Shield:** Ingestion manifest tracking (SHA-256, SPDX license, provenance), MinHash LSH deduplication, and 10-gram overlap scanning against test benchmarks (HumanEval+, MBPP+, LiveCodeBench, SWE-bench).
* **Multi-Stage Specialization Taxonomy:** First-class support for SFT, PEFT/LoRA, QLoRA, Continued Pretraining (CPT/DAPT), DPO, and GRPO (test-driven verifiable rewards).
* **Isolated Execution Sandbox:** Sandboxed code execution harness with strict memory caps, timeouts, and zero-network isolation.
* **Economic & Pareto Frontier Engine:** Multi-objective optimization quantifying domain gain ($\Delta \mathcal{S}_{\text{domain}}$), general capability retention ($\Delta \mathcal{S}_{\text{general}}$), and dollar cost ($).

---

## 3. Quickstart & Installation

```bash
# Clone and install ViForge in editable mode
git clone https://github.com/vfcarida/ViForge.git
cd ViForge
pip install -e .
```

### CLI Overview

```bash
# 1. List registered models
viforge list-models

# 2. List available training methods and benchmark plugins
viforge list-plugins

# 3. Profile memory and estimated cost before training
viforge profile configs/experiments/exp_002_deepseek_v4_pro_qlora_sft.yaml

# 4. Run full specialization experiment and evaluation
viforge run configs/experiments/exp_002_deepseek_v4_pro_qlora_sft.yaml
```

---

## 4. DeepSeek V4 Pro Reference Experiment Matrix

| Run ID | Model Base | Adaptation Strategy | Hardware | Est. Cost (AWS) | Primary Metric |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `exp_001` | DeepSeek V4 Pro | **Base Baseline** (Zero-shot) | 1× A100 | \$0.50 | Baseline Pass@1 |
| `exp_002` | DeepSeek V4 Pro | **QLoRA SFT (NF4 r=64)** | 1× A100 80GB | \$12.00 | $\Delta$ Pass@1 vs Base |
| `exp_003` | DeepSeek V4 Pro | **CPT + QLoRA + DPO** | 4× A100 80GB | \$166.00 | Multi-stage Compounding |

---

## 5. Repository Structure

```text
ViForge/
├── configs/
│   ├── models/                # Model cards (DeepSeek V4 Pro, Qwen 2.5 Coder, etc.)
│   └── experiments/           # Declarative experiment manifests (YAML)
├── viforge/
│   ├── core/                  # Schemas, interfaces, typed exceptions, structured logging
│   ├── registry/              # ModelRegistry, DatasetRegistry, PluginManager
│   ├── data/                  # Deduplication (MinHash), Contamination, Security (TruffleHog)
│   ├── synthetic/             # Task generation, AST verification, Rejection sampling
│   ├── training/              # Profilers, SFT, LoRA/QLoRA, CPT, DPO/GRPO, AdapterMerger
│   ├── inference/             # Unified generation client with seed pinning
│   ├── evaluation/            # Sandboxed test harness (HumanEval+, MBPP+, SWE-bench, MMLU-Pro)
│   ├── analysis/              # AWSCostModel, ParetoEngine, ReportGenerator
│   ├── infra/                 # AWS S3 sync & SageMaker runners
│   ├── orchestrator.py        # End-to-end experiment pipeline
│   └── cli.py                 # Typer & Rich CLI
└── tests/                     # Comprehensive test suite (Unit, Contract, Data, ML Regression)
```

---

## 6. Running Tests

```bash
pytest tests/ -v
```

